  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the minimum probabilities of the lotteries and selecting the one with the lower minimum probability (i.e., more 'extreme' low-probability event). While the individual does notice the 1% probability in Lottery A, it is interpreted as a risk to be avoided, not as a basis for comparing the structural property (minimum probability) of the two lotteries. The individual uses the 1% figure to assess risk tolerance and expected utility trade-offs, not to apply a rule based on extremal probability values. Furthermore, the individual appears to favor Lottery B, whereas the decision reason would favor Lottery A. The justification is based on risk-benefit evaluation, not on a formal comparison of minimum probabilities as a decisive criterion. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
